# Zensical docs build output
site/

# Superpowers scratch dir — plans/specs are never committed (see global operating-model rule)
docs/superpowers/

test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
blob-report/
data/e2e-test.db*
docker-data/

# .claude/settings.json and hooks/ ARE tracked: the PreToolUse guard has to
# enforce the Backlog.md rules (bare --notes/--plan replaces a section silently;
# hand-edited task markdown loses one at exit 0) for anyone working in this repo.
# Everything else under .claude/ is per-machine state: worktrees, scheduler locks,
# and settings.local.json.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/

.env2

# Injected by the m7kni.io hub at build time — never commit these.
# The hub copies its own SEO template, brand stylesheet and fonts into a clone
# and generates zensical.toml from docs.toml. A tracked copy here is drift, and
# is exactly what the manifest model exists to prevent.
/zensical.toml
docs/overrides/
docs/stylesheets/brand.css
docs/assets/project-icon.svg
docs/assets/project-icon-solid.svg
docs/assets/social-card.png
docs/assets/social-card.svg
docs/fonts/
